The venv exists but has no `pip` binary — it's broken. Recreate it:

```bash
deactivate
rm -rf venv
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
which pip
```

Confirm `which pip` shows the venv path, then:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install arize-phoenix
```

If `python3 -m venv venv` itself fails, you may need:

```bash
sudo apt install python3-venv python3-full
```

Then retry the venv creation.
